Subject: feat: reach the routes from the Space menu, and sort open tabs by
 them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Space menu gets two rows, above the colours. "Route sites here…" opens the
list of routes on that Space: chrome://settings/stedding?card=routes&space=<id>
brings the card into view, chooses that Space in the add row and puts the focus
in its field, using a Settings tab already open (routing D15).

"Sort open tabs by these rules now" moves this window's open tabs, from every
Space, to the Spaces their rules name, every kind of rule counted. An essential,
a Space pin, a tab in a folder and a tab in a split stay where they were put, a
rule naming no Space moves nothing, and the window stays on the Space it shows:
a tab that leaves it hands the selection on, and no Space comes on screen
unasked. With nothing to move the row is disabled and says "Nothing to move". The
card has the same words as a button, which says what it moved, and the command
bar has "Sort Open Tabs by Routes" while there is a tab to move (routing D16;
commandbar K40). A Blank Window's Space menu has neither row: no route moves a
tab there.

chrome://settings/stedding?card=<name> opens the page on the card of that name
(settings T57), which the command bar and the page after an Arc import go by too.

Why: the second pass of routing, which closes routing D5's partial state
(BACKLOG S-126, S-422).

Removable when: never as behaviour.
